;; repr/asm's cross-syntax judge's classes (bin/repr-asm encode-check; doc/asm/AMD64-SURVEY.md §5, §8.1, "As built: AX3"): every AT&T
;; instruction of test/asm/encode-results-amd64.edn's :cross rows that does not read back from its Intel print to the same machine
;; instruction is counted under its :by class, one of these (arbace.asm.amd64.check's cross-judge names the class by a rule on the
;; instruction and its print). The by-design classes are llvm-mc's own: its Intel printer writes text its Intel parser reads as another
;; instruction or rejects (each class's :oracle, llvm-mc 23.1.5 by hand: `-output-asm-variant=1`, then `-x86-asm-syntax=intel`). In
;; goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :ambiguous
  :title "an Intel print that names another instruction"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the instruction's Intel print is the very text another instruction prints, and the Intel parser takes the other: the _REV forms (`vmovups.s` prints `vmovups zmm2, zmm1`), the operand-size variants without a suffix (retw prints `ret`, popl %ss in 32-bit mode `pop ss`, read as POPSS16), an immediate printU8Imm masks to 8 bits (`bt eax, 255` for $-1), an absent index with a scale"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `vmovups.s %zmm1, %zmm2` prints `vmovups zmm2, zmm1` (0x11), read back 0x10; `pop ss` in i386 Intel encodes 0x66,0x17 (POPSS16), `ret 4` 0xc2 (RETI32)"
  :decided "AX3 (AXS34)"}
 {:id :other-instruction
  :title "an Intel print read back as another instruction"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the Intel print reads back as another instruction with another print: the far jumps and calls through memory print without their size (`call [rax]` for lcall *(%rax), read as a near call), a move from a segment register into a 16-bit register is read into the 32-bit one (parseInstruction's mov %seg rewrite)"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `lcall *(%rax)` prints `call [rax]`, read back `call qword ptr [rax]` (0xff,0x10); `movw %cs, %ax` prints `mov ax, cs`, read back `mov eax, cs`"
  :decided "AX3 (AXS34)"}
 {:id :pcrel-imm
  :title "a branch to a constant address"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "a branch whose target is a number (`je 0`): Intel syntax reads a bare number as an immediate, which no branch takes (printPCRelImm prints the immediate as it is)"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `je 0` in Intel syntax: `error: invalid operand for instruction`"
  :decided "AX3 (AXS34)"}
 {:id :disassemble-only
  :title "an instruction no matchable names"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "processInstruction's shift or rotate by 1 of an 8-bit register with APX's new data destination is ROL8r1_ND (and RCL, RCR, ROR, SAR, SHL, SHR, with or without {nf}), DisassembleOnly in X86InstrShiftRotate.td (its FIXME: the assembler cannot tell it from the rCL form): its Intel print `rol bl, al` no Intel matchable reads"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `rolb $1, %al, %bl` prints `rol bl, al` (-output-asm-variant=1); `rol bl, al` read in Intel syntax: `error: invalid operand for instruction`"
  :decided "AX2's fourth slice (AXS34's rule)"}
 {:id :mask-operand
  :title "a standalone mask operand"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "AVX512PF's gathers and scatters print their mask as an operand of its own (`vgatherpf0dps {k1}, dword ptr [r8 + zmm20]`), which parseIntelOperand takes for a rounding mode"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `vgatherpf0dps {k1}, dword ptr [r8 + zmm20]`: `error: unknown token in expression`"
  :decided "AX3 (AXS34)"}
 {:id :dollar-name
  :title "a symbol named with $"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "AT&T's `$foo` inside an expression is the symbol `$foo`; Intel syntax has no `$` (ParseIntelExpression's Dollar is MASM's)"
  :oracle "llvm-mc 23.1.5: `cmp edi, dword ptr [3+$foo@ABS8]`: `error: unknown token in expression`"
  :decided "AX3 (AXS34)"}
 {:id :local-label
  :title "a directional local label"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the operand names 1f or 1b, which the printer does not print yet (test/asm/divergences-print.edn's :local-label): none since 2026-11-17, the statement's label is the temporary symbol llvm-mc names it (.Ltmp0), printed in Intel and read back as that symbol"
  :decided "AX3, after the print level's class; emptied 2026-11-17 (h-asm-directive)"}
 {:id :dot
  :title "the location counter"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the operand names `.`, which the printer does not print yet"
  :decided "AX3, after the print level's class"}
 {:id :apx
  :title "APX"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the Intel print reads back to an instruction the matcher classes :apx"
  :decided "AX3"}
 {:id :intel-unread
  :title "an Intel print the reader refuses"
  :kind :pending
  :why "the Intel reader refuses the printed text: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :rejected
  :title "an Intel print the matcher rejects"
  :kind :pending
  :why "the Intel matcher rejects the printed text: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :mismatch
  :title "another machine instruction"
  :kind :pending
  :why "the Intel print reads back as the same instruction with other operands, and its print differs: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
 {:id :crash
  :title "the judge crashed"
  :kind :pending
  :why "an exception in the printer, the reader or the matcher: a failure to fix"
  :decided "a failure to fix"}
]
